# Upload filter for `railway up --no-gitignore`.
#
# WHY --no-gitignore IS NEEDED: deploy/artifacts/ is gitignored on purpose (199 MB
# of binaries, one file above GitHub's 100 MB limit), but the image must COPY it.
# `railway up` honours .gitignore by default, which would strip it from the
# upload, so the deploy command passes --no-gitignore and THIS file becomes the
# authoritative exclusion list.
#
# Because .gitignore is bypassed, the private directories are listed here FIRST
# and explicitly. Verify before deploying: the build log's upload size should be
# ~205 MB. If it is ~255 MB or more, context/ went along and you must stop the
# deploy.

# PRIVACY: real citizen data, never upload.
context/
outputs/

# The raw 415 MB artifacts directory; deploy/artifacts/ is what the image copies.
artifacts/

direcciones_ANN.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints/
scripts/
tests/
.atl/
.pytest_cache/
.git/
.github/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.env
